## Worksheet

**F1 (Core loop):** Single `game` object; `game.rng` (mulberry32) used for all randomness (no `Math.random` found); `endTurn()` resolves consumption→production→morale→trade→events→storms in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 (Map):** 8x8 grid (`initMap`, 64 tiles) with terrain from seeded rng; but `buildBuilding` is **defined twice** — the second definition (`buildBuilding.call({}, ...)`) shadows the first and recurses on itself infinitely, so buildings are never actually placed into `game.map.buildings`. `adjacencyBonus` data exists on `BUILDINGS` but is never read anywhere (not in `getProductionOutput`). Score 1.

**F3 (Economy):** Production/consumption chains (e.g. greenhouse consumes water→food) and cap/overflow logic exist in the turn loop, but they iterate `game.map.buildings`, which is permanently empty due to the F2 bug — never executes with real data. Score 1.

**F4 (Population):** Colonist records have skill/fatigue/morale/job (`addColonist`); `getProductionOutput` reads `colonist.skill` but only via `building.workers`, which is set to `[]` at creation and never populated by any code; fatigue is never read by production at all. Score 1.

**F5 (Needs):** `endTurn` consumes food/water and reduces `colonist.morale` on shortage; morale can recover via event effects (`morale_spike`); but morale is never read in `getProductionOutput`, so "morale changes output" is unmet. Score 1.

**F6 (Research):** 12 nodes, prereqs enforced in `canResearch`, costs deducted in `doResearch`; but `population_tech.prereqs` references nonexistent id `'community_programs'` causing a `TypeError` every time the research tab renders; only 3/12 nodes (`resilience_1/2`, `trade_tech`) have real code effects, rest are flavor text. Score 1.

**F7 (Events):** 10 events defined; 6 offer 2 choices with differing effects (`applyEventEffects`); cooldown field decremented each turn, but selection uses uniform `rngShuffle`, not weighted; `fired` Set permanently blocks repeats so events stop firing after 10 uses. Score 1.

**F8 (Trade):** `generateCaravan` prices from `game.trade.globalSupply` and player `game.resources` (demand mod); `trade()` handles both buy/sell; caravan quantity decremented and UI gates purchases via `maxBuy`. Score 2.

**F9 (Hazard):** `triggerAshstorm` fires periodically with severity scaling from turn count, and reads `resilience_1/2` research + `stormDamageReduction`; but it only damages entries in `game.map.buildings`, permanently empty (F2 bug); `repairBuilding` has **zero call sites** anywhere in the UI. Score 1.

**F10 (Save/load):** `saveGame` serializes full state to textarea; `loadGame` wraps `JSON.parse` + assignments in try/catch, alerts on error. Score 2.

**F11 (End conditions):** Win (`turn>=60 && colonists>=12`) and lose (`colonists.length===0`) both reachable (manual "Add Colonist" button bypasses broken buildings); `renderEndScreen` computes score from population/resources/research/turn. Score 2.

**F12 (UI):** Tab click listener switches panels; log entries carry `entry.turn`; keyboard shortcuts (`Space`, `Digit1-5`) wired via `keydown` listener; but `.two-column` responsive CSS class is never applied to any element, and no real "number origin" tooltips beyond tile info. Score 1.

**F13 (Dev panel):** `runTests()` has 15 real invariant checks (caps, prereqs, RNG determinism, save/load roundtrip); `runBenchmark()` runs 200 headless `endTurn()` calls and prints `getGameHash()`. Score 2.

**G1:** `getProductionOutput` never reads any `game.research.*` flag directly — no code path connects research unlocks to the yield formula. Score 0.

**G2:** Shortage genuinely mutates `colonist.morale` in `endTurn`, but morale is never read by `getProductionOutput` — final "reduced labor output" link absent. Score 1.

**G3:** `triggerAshstorm` damages `game.map.buildings` (empty due to F2 bug) and `getProductionOutput` reads `building.damage`, but no building ever exists, and `repairBuilding` is unreferenced by any UI element (dead code). Score 0.

**G4:** `generateCaravan` recomputes `finalPrice` from live `game.resources` (demandMod) each caravan cycle; `globalSupply` itself never drifts. Score 3.

**G5:** `applyEventEffects` mutates real state (food/morale/colonists/parts/scrip) differently per choice branch in `disease`/`wanderer`/`supply_shortage`; but `effects.fatigue` is never handled and `effects.production` loop body is empty (no-op). Score 3.

